# Otocac municipal cemetery, photographed 8 October 2024.
#
# 86 photographs taken at the churchyard below the parish church, read out
# 15 September 2026. GPS on the files puts them at 44 52 04.8 N, 15 15 22.44 E,
# altitude 459 m -- Otocac.
#
# HOW THIS DIFFERS FROM sources/findagrave/. Those rows are an INDEX: someone
# else's transcription of a memorial, where a date may be the cemetery's record
# rather than the stone. These rows are read off PHOTOGRAPHS OF THE STONES
# THEMSELVES, at full resolution. That is better evidence, and it is also the
# only surviving record for stones Find a Grave has never covered -- the
# Croatian cemeteries of this family are all empty there.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. A gravestone is a memorial, not a register. It is carved by
# the living, often decades after the death, and it is wrong often enough to
# matter -- the Senj stone in this archive gives Ljubomir's birth as 1891 where
# the register says 1892. Nothing here is joined to the tree on its own.
#
# "conf" is how sure the reading is: r = read cleanly, p = partly legible,
# ? = uncertain and not to be relied on.
#
# surname|given|born|died|stone|conf|photo
